hich of the following is true of ‘placebos’","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Placebo is a dummy medication"},{"label":"B","text":"Placebo is the inert material added to the drug for making tablets"},{"label":"C","text":"Placebos do not produce any effect"},{"label":"D","text":"All patients respond to placebos (p. 55)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"af4c4a0fd030f7b7e4f57118c0c2b38ce6177477"},{"id":"q-f214afceed34","stem":"51 In patients of hepatic cirrhosis","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Gastroenterology and Hepatology","topicOriginal":"Gastroenterology and Hepatology","subtopic":"Hepat","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The extent of change in pharmacokinetics of drugs can be predicted from the values of liver function tests"},{"label":"B","text":"High doses of furosemide can be safely used"},{"label":"C","text":"Metformin is the preferred oral hypoglycaemic"},{"label":"D","text":"Disposition of atenolol is not significantly affected (p. 56)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Gastroenterology and Hepatology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5557d4f62cef","stem":"52 In patients with renal insufficiency the clearance of the following drug is reduced parallel to the reduction in creatinine clearance","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Propranolol"},{"label":"B","text":"Digoxin"},{"label":"C","text":"Lignocaine"},{"label":"D","text":"Verapamil (p. 56)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-4ddab55eef7a","stem":"53 The following statement is not correct for uremic patients","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Attainment of steady-state plasma concentration of drugs eliminated through the kidney is hastened"},{"label":"B","text":"Pethidine can cause seizures"},{"label":"C","text":"Diazepam produces exaggerated CNS depression"},{"label":"D","text":"Tetracyclines further raise blood urea level (p. 56)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f7e664bb2be3","stem":"54 In congestive heart failure patients","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Cardiology","topicOriginal":"Cardiology","subtopic":"Heart","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Volume of distribution of all drugs is increased"},{"label":"B","text":"Hepatic clearance of drugs is unaffected"},{"label":"C","text":"Orally administered diuretics may not be effec- tive, but the same may work parenterally"},{"label":"D","text":"Inotropic action of digoxin is attenuated (p. 56-57)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Cardiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"7553497de22411757e96df05fd8f9450b0fdce71"},{"id":"q-285ecfe10fc9","stem":"55 Interaction between the following pair of drugs can be avoided by making suitable adjustments","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Levodopa and metoclopramide"},{"label":"B","text":"Furosemide and indomethacin"},{"label":"C","text":"Tetracyclines and ferrous sulfate"},{"label":"D","text":"Clonidine and chlorpromazine (p. 57, 670)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a5989a694efb","stem":"56 Drug cumulation is the basis of organ toxicity of the following drug when used for prolonged periods","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Prednisolone"},{"label":"B","text":"Chloroquine"},{"label":"C","text":"Aspirin"},{"label":"D","text":"Hydralazine (p. 58, 740)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAns