nomenon of","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Anesthesiology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Anaphylaxis"},{"label":"B","text":"Tachyphylaxis"},{"label":"C","text":"Idiosyncrasy"},{"label":"D","text":"Drug resistance (p. 59)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Anesthesiology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"6422ae108cf77329940d787644dfcceac90e0b90"},{"id":"q-6f3825b740d8","stem":"1 An undesirable effect of a drug that occurs at thera- peutic doses and can be predicted from its pharma- cological actions is called","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Side effect"},{"label":"B","text":"Toxic effect"},{"label":"C","text":"Allergic reaction"},{"label":"D","text":"Idiosyncrasy (p. 61)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b622bd0530bc","stem":"2 Which of the following is a type B (unpredictable) adverse drug reaction","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Side effect"},{"label":"B","text":"Toxic effect"},{"label":"C","text":"Idiosyncrasy"},{"label":"D","text":"Physical dependence (p. 60, 62)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f9b5d4e5c0fc","stem":"3 The side effect of a drug which has been used as a therapeutic effect in another condition is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Constipation caused by codeine"},{"label":"B","text":"Cough caused by captopril"},{"label":"C","text":"Uterine stimulation caused by quinine"},{"label":"D","text":"Diarrhoea caused by ampicillin (p. 61)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-34344c55e856","stem":"4 A ‘toxic effect’ differs from a ‘side effect’ in that","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is not a pharmacological effect of the drug"},{"label":"B","text":"It is a more intense pharmacological effect that occurs at high dose or after prolonged medication"},{"label":"C","text":"It must involve drug induced cellular injury"},{"label":"D","text":"It involves host defence mechanisms (p. 61)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d9e16dcb836a","stem":"5 The following statement is true in relation to ‘drug toxicity’ and ‘poisoning’","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The two terms are synonymous"},{"label":"B","text":"When a toxic effect requires specific treat- ment, it is called poisoning"},{"label":"C","text":"A toxic effect which endangers life by markedly affecting vital functions is called poisoning"},{"label":"D","text":"Toxicity is caused by drugs while poisoning is caused by other harmful chemicals (p. 61, 62)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"225f99998302ffc0fc83f99b46fa84a26172daf3"},{"id":"q-10ba0cfc230f","stem":"6 Use of an emetic to remove the ingested poison is contraindicated in following poisonings except that by","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Strychnine"},{"label":"B","text":"Caustic soda"},{"label":"C","text":"Ferrous sulfate"},{"label":"D","text":"Kerosene (p. 62, 600)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0fb7cc3743e5","stem":"7 Which of the following is an idiosyncratic adverse drug reaction","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Muscle dystonia caused by triflupromazine"},{"label":"B","text":"Insomnia after taking pentobarbitone"},{"label":"C","text":"Precipitation of asthma by morphine"},{"label":"D","text":"Gum hyperplasia caused by phenytoin (p. 62)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7b098303c406","stem":"8 An immunologically mediated reaction to a drug pro- ducing stereotyped symptoms unrelated to its pharma- codynamic actions is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Hypersensitivity"},{"label":"B","text":"Supersensitivity"},{"label":"C","text":"Intolerance"},{"label":"D","text":"Idiosyncrasy (p. 62, 63)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independent_no_source_key_bulk_v4","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f99add7bfc60","stem":"9 Drugs producing allergic reactions generally act as","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOrigina