obe of the brain"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-67e45f3b012b","stem":"Isoniazid is eliminated rapidly in some people but slower in others because","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Of hereditary variation in the rate of isoniazid excretion by the kidneys"},{"label":"B","text":"Of a variable capacity of the hepatic enzyme acetyltransferase to metabolise isoniazid"},{"label":"C","text":"Pseudocholinesterase enzymes exhibit a form of polymorphism"},{"label":"D","text":"The enzyme glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase exists in at least two polymorphic forms"},{"label":"E","text":"Isoniazid polymerase is absent in some individuals"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a546b4ae84e3","stem":"Which of the following statements is INCORRECT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Some histamine H1 receptor antagonists are used in the prophylaxis and treatment of motion sickness"},{"label":"B","text":"Histamine H2 receptor antagonists are potentially useful in the treatment of gastric hypersecretory states"},{"label":"C","text":"Promethazine possesses anti-emetic, sedative and anti-muscarinic activity"},{"label":"D","text":"Histamine H1 receptor antagonists inhibit the release of histamine"},{"label":"E","text":"Histamine H1 receptor antagonists are effective in the treatment of hay fever Page 1 of 19 By Duy Thai, 1997 www.geocities.com/d.thai"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"a09e939eb72ba527775ee65cdc175f40412b8203"},{"id":"q-a0d0cc8e6e80","stem":"The antihypertensive action of prazosin is due to","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Cardiovascular Drugs","topicOriginal":"Cardiovascular Drugs","subtopic":"Antihypertensive","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Blockade of calcium channels."},{"label":"B","text":"Inhibition of angiotensin converting enzyme."},{"label":"C","text":"Antagonism of alpha1-adrenoceptors"},{"label":"D","text":"Inhibition of transmitter release from noradrenergic nerve terminals."},{"label":"E","text":"Selective depression of cardiac output."}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Cardiovascular Drugs","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a89b16e351c1","stem":"Which of the following statements about glyceryl trinitrate is INCORRECT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","tex