ich of the following is NOT associated with treatment of cancer patients with an alkylating agent","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Nausea"},{"label":"B","text":"Hair loss"},{"label":"C","text":"A rapid decline in erythrocyte count"},{"label":"D","text":"A decline in white blood cell numbers"},{"label":"E","text":"Degeneration of intestinal crypts"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a1302c6795ed","stem":"Bromocriptine is NOT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"An ergot derivative"},{"label":"B","text":"A dopamine agonist"},{"label":"C","text":"A prolactin antagonist"},{"label":"D","text":"Effective by mouth"},{"label":"E","text":"Capable of causing mental disturbances such as psychosis and/or mania"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-efbaa2fc4947","stem":"Potent inhalational anaesthetics such as halothane","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Anesthesiology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Have analgesic properties at subanaesthetic concentrations"},{"label":"B","text":"Cause dose dependent liver damage"},{"label":"C","text":"Limit the inspired oxygen concentration that can be delivered"},{"label":"D","text":"Are bronchodilators"},{"label":"E","text":"Reduce cerebral blood flow"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Anesthesiology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f2e36501b6a3","stem":"Which of the following statements is INCORRECT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Dopa decarboxylase is present in noradrenaline storage vesicle"},{"label":"B","text":"Tyrosine hydroxylase is present in the cytoplasm of sympathetic nerve varicosities"},{"label":"C","text":"Monoamine oxidase is associated with mitochondrial membrane in sympathetic nerve varicosities"},{"label":"D","text":"Catechol-o-methyltransferase is present in smooth muscle cells"},{"label":"E","text":"Dopamine β hydroxylase is present in noradrenaline storage vesicles Page 3 of 19 By Duy Thai, 1997 www.geocities.com/d.thai"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"a09e939eb72ba527775ee65cdc175f40412b8203"},{"id":"q-9de5cf0d48e2","stem":"Which of the following inhalational anaesthetics is most likely to produce hepatotoxicity","type":"Single B