"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"They may pass through the small aqueous channels in cell membranes"},{"label":"B","text":"They generally do not gain access to cells within the brain except by specific transport mechanisms"},{"label":"C","text":"They cross cell membranes less readily than do non-ionised drugs"},{"label":"D","text":"Such drugs include the general anaesthetic thiopentone"},{"label":"E","text":"Such drugs include the cytokine granulocyte colony stimulating factor (G-CSF)"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-18499640d2c1","stem":"Which of the following actions of noradrenaline is due to activation of α receptors","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"General Pharmacology","topicOriginal":"General Pharmacology","subtopic":"Receptor","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Dilation of blood vessels in skeletal muscles"},{"label":"B","text":"Bronchodilation"},{"label":"C","text":"Dilation of the pupil"},{"label":"D","text":"Enhanced release of renin from the juxtaglomerular cells of the kidney"},{"label":"E","text":"Relaxation of the uterus"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"General Pharmacology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-453d99732421","stem":"Which statements about antiarrhythmic drugs is INCORRECT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Cardiovascular Drugs","topicOriginal":"Cardiovascular Drugs","subtopic":"Antiarrhythmic","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"In the treatment of certain supraventricular arrhythmias, lignocaine may be administered orally"},{"label":"B","text":"Tissue accumulation of amiodarone leads to a range of adverse effects"},{"label":"C","text":"In high doses, lignocaine may cause disorientation, convulsions and respiratory arrest"},{"label":"D","text":"Verapamil is useful for the treatment of atrial, but not ventricular arrhythmias"},{"label":"E","text":"Lignocaine is used almost exclusively to treat ventricular arrhythmias"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Cardiovascular Drugs","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-14aa1c25d93b","stem":"Calcium antagonists exert their effects primarily by","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Inhibiting cyclic nucleotide phosphodiesterases"},{"label":"B","text":"Blocking Na+/K+ ATPase"},{"label":"C","text":"Enhancing the binding of intracellular Ca2+ to sarcoplasmic reticulum"},{"label":"D","text":"Inhibiting transport through Ca2+ channels in the plasma membrane"},{"label":"E","text":"Blocking the Na+ influx associated with the rising phase of the action potential Page 4 of 19 By Duy Thai, 1997 www.geocities.com/d.thai"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_n