n of the free drug"},{"label":"E","text":"Metabolism in the liver"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Upper Limb","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-41fee3a3de3c","stem":"Intravenous administration","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Is too slow for emergency use"},{"label":"B","text":"Cannot be used with unconscious patients"},{"label":"C","text":"Usually produces a slower response than does oral administration"},{"label":"D","text":"Generally results in more precisely determined effects than does oral administration"},{"label":"E","text":"Is the cheapest route for drug administration Page 14 of 19 By Duy Thai, 1997 www.geocities.com/d.thai"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-78a022963eb3","stem":"The selectivity of acyclovir for certain Herpes viruses is due primarily to","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Its selectivity for the viral reverse transcriptase enzyme"},{"label":"B","text":"Its irreversible inhibition of Herpes DNA polymerase"},{"label":"C","text":"Its structural similarity to the nucleoside thymidine"},{"label":"D","text":"Its selectivity for Herpes DNA polymerase"},{"label":"E","text":"Inhibition of translation of viral proteins"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"newly_reasoned_provisional","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-332a092bb898","stem":"Which of the following statements about captopril is INCORRECT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It inhibits the conversion of the decapeptide angiotensin I to the octapeptide angiotensin II"},{"label":"B","text":"It inhibits the synthesis of substance P"},{"label":"C","text":"It inhibits the inactivation of bradykinin"},{"label":"D","text":"It is well absorbed orally"},{"label":"E","text":"It is used as an antihypertensive drug"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6be43decc4bb","stem":"Which of the following antacid drugs as all these properties: (a) is non systemic, (b) is neutralising, (c) is liable to cause constipation","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sodium bicarbonate"},{"label":"B","text":"Magnesium hydroxide"},{"label":"C","text":"Magnesium trisilicate"},{"label":"D","text":"Aluminium hydroxide"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a2a039d41b12","stem":"Acyclovir is not","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Active against herpes simplex type I"},{"label":"B","text":"Given orally"},{"label":"C","text":"Active against herpes simplex type II"},{"label":"D","text":"A purine analogue"},{"label":"E","text":"A pyrimidine analogue"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-89d00f39b660","stem":"The side effects associated with tricyclic antidepressant therapy DO NOT include","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Central Nervous System Drugs","topicOriginal":"Central Nervous System Drugs","subtopic":"Antidepressant","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Tachycardia"},{"label":"B","text":"Dry mouth"},{"label":"C","text":"Sweating"},{"label":"D","text":"Hypertension"},{"label":"E","text":"Blurred vision Page 15 of 19 By Duy Thai, 1997 www.geocities.com/d.thai"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Central Nervous System Drugs","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-6e52494b14bf","stem":"The anti anginal vasodilator drug GTN is administered as a transdermal patch or sublingual tablet rather than via the oral (swallowed) route because","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is not absorbed across the mucous membranes of the stomach or intestines"},{"label":"B","text":"It causes severe vomiting"},{"label":"C","text":"It enters an enterohepatic shunt"},{"label":"D","text":"It is rapidly metabolised by the liver"},{"label":"E","text":"It is destroyed by the bacterial flora of the gastrointestinal tract"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c0472660ce4b","stem":"Low doses of aspirin can be used to selectively block platelet cycloooxygenase (COX) over the enzyme in arterial endothelial cells because","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Platelet COX is acetylated by aspirin more quickly than that of arterial endothelial cells"},{"label":"B","text":"The platelet enzyme is irreversibly inhibited, while the endothelial enzyme is reversibly inhibited"},{"label":"C","text":"Endothelial cells can resynthesise COX and hence recover from aspirin quickly"},{"label":"D","text":"Aspirin is a pro drug and platelets rapidly convert aspirin to its active form"},{"label":"E","text":"Aspirin has a very long half life"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerifie