al reuptake of transmitter noradrenaline"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-619cbaad91e9","stem":"The bioavailability of a preparation of a drug is a measure of","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Pharmacokinetics and Dynamics · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Pharmacokinetics and Dynamics","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The relative toxicity of the preparation to laboratory animals"},{"label":"B","text":"The stability of the preparation"},{"label":"C","text":"The proportion of active drug appearing in the plasma"},{"label":"D","text":"The acceptability of the preparation to the patient"},{"label":"E","text":"The availability of the drug from natural sources Page 17 of 19 By Duy Thai, 1997 www.geocities.com/d.thai"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Pharmacokinetics and Dynamics · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-d4a41d901f27","stem":"Which of the following statements about imipramine is INCORRECT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It can produce tachycardia and cardiac arrhythmias"},{"label":"B","text":"It antagonises some of the actions of histamine"},{"label":"C","text":"It can produce dry mouth"},{"label":"D","text":"Has alpha adrenergic properties"},{"label":"E","text":"It is an antidepressant and a potent inhibitor of monoamine oxidase"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-9a3374a008f6","stem":"H2 autoreceptors on mast cells","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"General Pharmacology","topicOriginal":"General Pharmacology","subtopic":"Receptor","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Increase degranulation by mobilising calcium"},{"label":"B","text":"Cause PLC (phopholipase C) activation"},{"label":"C","text":"Stimulate cAMP and inhibits degranulation"},{"label":"D","text":"Are readily blocked by promethazine"},{"label":"E","text":"Are located on intracellular calcium stores"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"General Pharmacology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-462094ce5954","stem":"Fenclonine and fluoxetine are useful to treat some CNS disorders because they increase serotonin levels in the synapse of serotonergic neurones","type":"True / False","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"True"},{"label":"B","text":"False"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated