ases that hydrolyze the lactone ring."},{"label":"E","text":"Formation of acetyl transferase that inactivates macrolides. Key: b Page 7 of 10 BDS SECOND PROFESSIONAL EXAMINATION 2007 PHARMACOLOGY AND DENTAL MATERIA MEDICA (MCQs) Model Paper"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-c6ceaa743d1f","stem":"Doxycycline is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bactericidal."},{"label":"B","text":"Not excreted in the feces."},{"label":"C","text":"Having a short elimination half-life."},{"label":"D","text":"Not effective in lyme disease."},{"label":"E","text":"Not as effective as tetracycline against H.pylori. Key: e"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["short_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1224a87877f0","stem":"Neomycin, an aminoglycoside is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Antimicrobials","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Least nephrotoxic."},{"label":"B","text":"Metabolized by hepatic enzyme."},{"label":"C","text":"Used in hepatic coma."},{"label":"D","text":"A drug of choice in Rockey Mountain Spotted fever."},{"label":"E","text":"An adjunct in treatment